   "evidence": "Mathlib/FieldTheory/IsRealClosed/Basic.lean:8-11 imports only Polynomial/Semireal/LinearCombination, so `\u211d` currently comes via the analysis imports. Repo convention: code/TauCeti/NumberTheory/LocalField/Herbrand.lean:8-11 uses `public import` for signature dependencies and plain `import` for proof-only Mathlib modules (`Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.DominatedConvergence`, `Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/FieldTheory/IsRealClosed/Real.lean",
   "fix": "Keep `public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsRealClosed.Basic`, add `public import Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic` (since `IsRealClosed.Basic` does not provide `\u211d`), and change the two analysis imports to plain `import`.",
   "issue": "`Mathlib.Analysis.Polynomial.Order` and `Mathlib.Analysis.Real.Sqrt` are `public import` but are used only inside the proof (`Real.isSquare_iff` and the four `Polynomial.*_leadingCoeff_*` sign lemmas); the statement `IsRealClosed \u211d` needs only `IsRealClosed` and `\u211d`. This re-exports real analysis and polynomial order theory to every importer of the module.",
   "line": 8
  }
 ],
